# Copy to /etc/hoanglong-bo/staging.env on the VPS, root:root 0600. NEVER committed.
#
# Outside the git tree on purpose, and named explicitly by every compose command
# (`--env-file /etc/hoanglong-bo/staging.env`). The old instruction pointed at
# /opt/hoanglong-bo/.env, which compose never read: it looks beside the compose
# file, one directory further down, and does not walk upwards.
#
#   POSTGRES_PASSWORD="$(openssl rand -hex 24)"
#
# HEX, NOT BASE64, and not for looks. This value is interpolated into
# DATABASE_URL as postgres://user:PASSWORD@host/db, and base64's alphabet
# includes "/", which ends the userinfo component and makes the URL
# unparseable. Measured: 39.7% of `openssl rand -base64 24` outputs contain one.
# Hex is 24 bytes either way - 192 bits - just spelled in an alphabet a URI
# cannot misread.
#
# Nothing here reaches the frontend bundle: the client is served as static files
# and talks to /api on its own origin.
POSTGRES_USER=backoffice
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=
POSTGRES_DB=backoffice
LOG_LEVEL=log
# The docker bridge nginx's upstream arrives from. Widen only with a measured
# reason — see TRUSTED_PROXIES in backend/src/config/env.schema.ts.
TRUSTED_PROXIES=172.16.0.0/12

# Address search on the location form, so a place gets the coordinates the
# driver's arrival is measured against. A SERVER key — it never reaches the
# bundle, unlike the browser map key this replaced. Get one at account.goong.io.
#
# Leaving it empty is safe and supported: the suggestion box says it is
# unavailable, and the map (OpenStreetMap, no key of its own) plus the two
# coordinate fields still locate a place. What it costs is the convenient path,
# not the only one.
GOONG_API_KEY=

# The MAP's tiles — the pictures, not the addresses. Fetched by the backend and
# served from our own origin at /api/tiles, because the browser could not reach
# the tile server: production drew a correct, fully initialised Leaflet map with
# every tile missing, while the same URL answered normally from a developer's
# machine. Moving the fetch is the whole fix and it needs no account — the
# default below is OpenStreetMap, which this process reaches fine.
#
# Leaving these empty is safe and supported. Setting them is the upgrade off
# donated infrastructure, and the attribution must change WITH the URL — it is
# a licence term, and it is served to the page rather than compiled into it.
#   MapTiler  https://api.maptiler.com/maps/streets-v2/{z}/{x}/{y}.png?key={key}
#   Stadia    https://tiles.stadiamaps.com/tiles/osm_bright/{z}/{x}/{y}.png?api_key={key}
#MAP_TILES_URL=
#MAP_TILES_KEY=
#MAP_TILES_ATTRIBUTION=
#MAP_TILES_MAX_ZOOM=
